  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Pennsylvania totaled $696M in FY2027 to date. The award count is 2,291 and the average award size is $304K. Obligations fell 97.5% year over year. Department-level concentration is high: the Department of Energy accounted for $372M and the Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $232M, which together represent the bulk of FY2027 to date obligations. Vendor concentration is also high: FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC received $373M and RICHARD GROUP LLC received $64.9M. Industry concentration shows Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) as the top NAICS, with $375M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $115M. Historical context shows prior fiscal years were substantially larger: FY26 obligations were $28.3B and FY25 obligations were $30.1B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2027 to date spending pattern in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy and the Department of Veterans Affairs dominate FY2027 to date spending, with $372M and $232M respectively. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC is the single largest vendor with $373M, which concentrates a large share of the state total. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry by obligations at $375M. Obligations fell 97.5% year over year, showing a sharp drop in current-year partial totals compared with prior full fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How do FY2027 to date awards compare to recent full fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $696M, well below recent full-year totals such as FY26 at $28.3B and FY25 at $30.1B. The award count is 2,291 and the average award size is $304K, which reflects the current-year partial reporting period. Historical results show much larger annual obligations in prior years, with FY24 at $29.8B, FY23 at $27.1B, and FY22 at $20.8B."
      }
    ]
  },
